{
  "message": "I can file this dispute for you. To do so I need to verify your identity and collect a few transaction details. Verification: I need you to confirm any 2 of the following (one should be your email so I can look up your account): - Email (please provide) - Date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY) - Phone number on file - Home address After verification I will look up your card and the transaction and file the dispute. Transaction details I need from you now: 1) Transaction date (MM/DD/YYYY) 2) Transaction amount (exact $ amount) 3) When you first noticed the issue (MM/DD/YYYY) — if that’s today, just say so 4) Do you want a full refund? (I assume yes — reply “yes” to confirm) 5) Do you want your card cancelled/reissued? (If no, I will set card_action = \"keep_active\") You mentioned you called the hotel twice and they refused to help — thank you, that satisfies the “contacted_merchant” requirement for non-fraud disputes. Note about provisional credit: Because this is a “goods/services not as described” dispute (you got a different room type), provisional credit is generally NOT eligible under our guidelines. If you’d like me to proceed, please reply with: - Your email AND one other verification item (DOB, phone, or address) - The transaction date and amount - The date you noticed the issue - Confirm you want a full refund and that I should keep the card active Once you send those, I will verify your identity and then file the dispute on your behalf. If you’d prefer to talk to a human instead at any point, say so and I can transfer you."
}

